cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these scripts, please cite the accompanying article."
title: "Guaranteed bounds on the local dose around magnetic nanoparticle clusters: computational scripts"
authors:
  - family-names: Talleb
    given-names: Hakeim
    affiliation: "Sorbonne Universite, CNRS, Laboratoire de Genie Electrique et Electronique de Paris (GeePs)"
    email: hakeim.talleb@sorbonne-universite.fr
abstract: >-
  Scripts reproducing every number, table and figure of the article "How much does averaged dose
  underestimate the local dose? Guaranteed bounds on the specific absorption rate and temperature
  rise around magnetic nanoparticle clusters". Guaranteed two-sided bounds on the local specific
  absorption rate and on the local temperature rise, from the Prager-Synge complementary variational
  principle on dual meshes with goal-oriented refinement, extended to the steady Pennes bioheat
  equation.
keywords:
  - magnetic nanoparticle hyperthermia
  - thermal dose
  - guaranteed error bounds
  - Prager-Synge
  - Pennes bioheat equation
  - certified computation
